**suggestion (bug_risk):** No automatic invocation of cleanup may lead to memory growth over time.

Integrate a mechanism to invoke cleanup periodically in long-running processes to avoid memory leaks.

Suggested implementation:

```typescript
  /**
   * Clear old metrics and errors (housekeeping)
   */
  private _cleanupInterval: NodeJS.Timeout | null = null;

  /**
   * Start periodic cleanup to avoid memory leaks in long-running processes.
   * Call this method after instantiating the monitor.
   * @param intervalMs Interval in milliseconds (default: 1 hour)
   */
  startPeriodicCleanup(intervalMs: number = 60 * 60 * 1000) {
    if (this._cleanupInterval) return; // Already started
    this._cleanupInterval = setInterval(() => this.cleanup(), intervalMs);
  }

  /**
   * Stop periodic cleanup (for graceful shutdown)
   */
  stopPeriodicCleanup() {
    if (this._cleanupInterval) {
      clearInterval(this._cleanupInterval);
      this._cleanupInterval = null;
    }
  }

```

You should call `startPeriodicCleanup()` after instantiating your monitor class, e.g.:
```js
const monitor = new CometAPIMonitor();
monitor.startPeriodicCleanup();
```
And call `stopPeriodicCleanup()` before process exit if needed.

